  "policyPrivacyBody": "WHAT WE COLLECT\nYour name and email from the sign-in provider you choose, and your gender only if you choose to give it (it is shown to nobody else). The school or class you belong to and your role in it. Lessons, the work you are set and hand in, each earlier hand-in, your marks and the history of any change to them, your attendance, pastoral notes, and your own notebook. Messages, voice notes, announcements and meeting links inside the app. Files you upload. Your subscriptions and notification settings.\n\nWHY\nTo run your classes, to keep your account secure, to bill subscriptions, and to meet legal duties. We do not sell personal data. We show no advertising. We do not use your data to train any AI model.\n\nMARKS AND ATTENDANCE\nTeachers can mark work done on paper as well as work handed in online. A mark is a draft that only your teachers can see until the teacher publishes it; a missing mark is never counted as zero. If a published mark is corrected, we keep the old mark, the new one, who changed it, when and why, and you and your parents are told if the mark changed. Attendance changes after the lesson's day need a reason, only the class's lead teacher can change a register more than seven days old, and every change is kept. Deadlines are set in your school's time zone.\n\nWHO SEES YOUR WORK\nYour class's teachers, and a parent linked to you once a mark is published. There is no school administrator in this version of the app. Other students cannot see your marks, your work or your private messages. Messages are stored on our servers and are not end-to-end encrypted.\n\nPARENTS AND CHILDREN\nA parent asks to be linked to a student, and the student approves or declines it on their own device. A parent may also create and manage an account for a child with no email or phone, and accepts these terms for the child. A linked parent sees published marks, attendance, work and class material, and can hand work in for a young child, but cannot change marks or attendance and is not given the child's private messages. Family+ is a paid plan for parents that covers up to 4 or up to 8 linked children, earliest linked first. For each child it covers it summarises what the parent can already see - marks by class, trends, attendance, missing work and missed tests - compares the child only with their own earlier record, and uses no AI.\n\nAI STUDY TOOLS\nThese tools are optional. When you use them, what you give them is sent to Together AI, an AI company outside Studafy: the question you type and the recent turns of the same chat, and - if you choose - a lesson's text, your own notes, or a photo you add (the study helper, whiteboard notes, lesson notes, quizzes and flashcards). Your name, email, school and marks are never sent. Chats are kept only on your device. Answers can be wrong, so never hand them in as your own work. AI never marks your work.\n\nFILES\nFiles are stored privately, scanned before anyone can download them, and opened only through links that work once and expire within minutes. Hidden details are removed from photos and voice notes. If a teacher replaces or removes a file, the class no longer sees it, but it is kept for the school.\n\nPAYMENTS\nStudafy Plus, Studafy Max and Family+ are charged by Apple or Google under their own terms. We never see your card.\n\nWHO ELSE PROCESSES DATA\nSupabase hosts the database, sign-in and files; Fly.io hosts the app; Axiom keeps its technical logs and Sentry its error reports; GitHub stores encrypted backups it cannot read; Redis holds short-lived counters; Google, Microsoft and Apple verify sign-in; Cloudflare runs a bot check; Together AI runs the AI study tools; Resend sends email and Firebase sends push notifications, which never contain your marks or messages; meetings happen in Google Meet. Each acts only on our instructions.\n\nWHERE YOUR DATA IS\nData may be processed outside your country, including outside the EEA, protected by Standard Contractual Clauses or an adequacy decision.\n\nWHAT WE CANNOT DELETE\nRecords of significant actions are append-only: nobody can edit them, including us, and they are deleted only when their retention period ends. This includes the history of marks and attendance, earlier hand-ins, and files a teacher replaced. Schools are often required to keep attendance, assessment and safeguarding records. The app shows you which records stay with your school before you confirm a deletion. Encrypted backups are kept for 30 days.\n\nON YOUR DEVICE\nThe app keeps your session, your language, a cache of what you opened and downloaded, your study helper chats and your profile photo, separately for each account. Your profile photo is never uploaded to our servers, so nobody else sees it. They are cleared when that account signs out.\n\nHOW WE PROTECT IT\nAccess to a class's data is enforced in the database itself, and only that class's teachers can change its marks and attendance. Secrets are stripped from logs. In our own records IP addresses are stored only as a one-way hash; the sign-in service (Supabase) keeps the IP address of a sign-in for up to 7 days. Backups are encrypted before they leave our systems.\n\nYOUR RIGHTS\nYou may ask for a copy of your data, correct it, delete your account, restrict or object to processing, or withdraw consent. Account deletion and data export are in Account settings, and deletion can be cancelled for 14 days; a parent does this for a child account they manage. You may complain to the Data Protection Commission in Ireland at any time.\n\nIf your school controls your records, ask your school first; we will pass your request on and tell you we have.",
